### 4.4. Evaluation Metrics

Each annotator saw N=10N=10 emission tables, each with a pre-annotation (PA). The annotator’s task is to correct incorrect pre-annotations and leave correct pre-annotations unchanged. Thus, we define:

N=10N=10

* • NN - Number of instances (emission tables) annotated. * • CC - Number of correctly pre-annotated instances. * • II - Number of incorrectly pre-annotated instances. * • CCC\_{C} - Number of correct PAs annotated as correct. * • COC\_{O} - Number of correct PAs falsely annotated as incorrect (overcorrection). * • ICI\_{C} - Number of incorrect PAs annotated as incorrect. * • IUI\_{U} - Number of incorrect PAs annotated as correct (undercorrection).

